Notebook[{Cell["ToPython", "ObjectName"], Cell["ToPython[out] generates a \
standalone NumPy (default) or mpmath Python module that evaluates the outputs \
of the ModelOutput out, with validated inputs and finite checked results.", 
   "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], Cell["ToPython[out] generates a \
standalone Python module of the ModelOutput out: evaluate(params, \
fields=None) returns every output as an ordered dict, and one function per \
output takes the same inputs. params is a sequence of complex values in the \
order of parameter_ids; fields maps required field IDs to full component \
vectors.", "Notes"], Cell["Inputs are validated (types, lengths, field keys, \
finite values) with TypeError or ValueError; a non-finite output or a domain \
error (singular point, Surd of a nonreal number) raises EvaluationError \
naming the output. Powers use Wolfram's principal complex branch, Surd the \
real root; exact constants are evaluated at the working precision. The module \
never uses eval or exec and changes no global precision.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options: PythonBackend (\"NumPy\" at machine precision, or \"mpmath\" \
with WorkingPrecision digits in a private context per call), \
WorkingPrecision, FunctionNames, ParameterNames, CommonSubexpressions. \
Nothing is imported or executed by ToPython.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Stage 9: ToPython also accepts ModularFormOutput and modular model \
outputs (tau_point, q_point, evaluate(params, point, fields, form_values), \
evaluate_report) with FormEvaluation, ExportEvaluationMethod, SeriesOrder, \
AccuracyGoal, PrecisionGoal, MaxSeriesOrder, TimeLimit and RequireProof; \
finite-group modules are unchanged. Accuracy and precision goals stay at \
least two digits below the backend digits; estimated errors never fall below \
the roundoff of the values and are propagated through model outputs.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["For modular outputs, RequireProof -> True currently fails \
with ProofRequired: no implemented route produces a Proven form (there is no \
exact identity certificate, and the S check is sampled).", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options (shared configured settings can override these defaults):", 
   "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["PythonBackend"], "TableText"], Cell["\"NumPy\"", 
        "TableText"], Cell["\"NumPy\" (default; complex128 arrays at machine \
precision) or \"mpmath\" (mpmath values in a private context with \
WorkingPrecision digits per call; matrices as nested lists). Other values \
fail with InvalidOption.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["WorkingPrecision"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["FunctionNames"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["<||>", "TableText"], Cell["Explicit names must be \
unique valid identifiers that are not reserved by the module (for example \
evaluate, manifest or Python keywords).", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["ParameterNames"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["<||>", "TableText"], Cell["<||> (default: each \
parameter's label, sanitized and made unique) or an association from \
parameter IDs to identifiers. Unknown IDs, invalid or duplicate identifiers \
fail with InvalidOption.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["CommonSubexpressions"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["True", "TableText"], 
       Cell["True (default) or False (every output written in full).", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["FormEvaluation"], "TableText"], Cell["\"Embedded\"", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Default \"Embedded\" (needs every used slot bound \
with resolved coefficients); External reports UnknownExternalError and is \
incompatible with RequireProof.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["ExportEvaluationMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Default Automatic; FiniteSeries \
reports a finite approximation without a tail bound and refuses accuracy \
goals.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["SeriesOrder"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic (default: chosen from the accuracy goal \
and the point, or 6 orders for construction checks) or a positive integer; an \
explicit order is required to evaluate a finite jet (the result then has \
EstimatedError Missing[\"NoTailBound\"] or the next-order difference).", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["AccuracyGoal"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["PrecisionGoal"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["MaxSeriesOrder"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["2000", "TableText"], Cell["2000 (default) or a positive integer; \
reaching it fails with ConvergenceFailure and the best estimate.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["TimeLimit"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["600", "TableText"], Cell["600 (default), a \
positive number or Infinity; exceeding it fails with TimeLimit and changes \
nothing.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["RequireProof"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["False", "TableText"], Cell["False (default) or True: a result \
that is not Proven (numerical fits, verified reconstructions, sampled checks) \
fails with ProofRequired.", "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> 
      {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.02], Scaled[0.3], Scaled[0.18], 
         Scaled[0.5]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"], 
  Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["PrepareModelOutput", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"PrepareModelOutput.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["PythonSource", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"PythonSource.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["PythonManifest", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"PythonManifest.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["ExportPython", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"ExportPython.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["PythonBackend", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"PythonBackend.nb", None}]}], "SeeAlso"], 
  Cell["Examples Initialization", "ExamplesInitializationSection"], 
  Cell["Open this notebook in its repository location. GAP must be installed; \
LINS is required for its bounded search page. Evaluate the setup before the \
examples.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"Get", "[", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Nest", "[", RowBox[{"DirectoryName", 
                  ",", RowBox[{"NotebookFileName", "[", "]"}], ",", "5"}], 
                "]"}], ",", "\"Kernel\"", ",", "\"init.m\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], ";"}]], "ExampleInitialization"], 
  Cell["Basic Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "=", RowBox[{"BuildGroup", 
                "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"GroupPresentation", "[", RowBox[
                     {RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s\"", ",", "\"t\""}], "}"}], 
                      ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s^2\"", ",", "\"t^2\"", 
                          ",", "\"(s.t)^3\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            ",", "d", ",", "l", ",", "r", ",", "m", ",", "mass"}], "}"}], 
        ",", RowBox[{RowBox[{"d", "=", RowBox[{"First", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Select", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                    "\"IrrepOrder\"", "]"}], ",", RowBox[{RowBox[
                     {RowBox[{"RepDim", "[", RowBox[{"GroupRepresentation", 
                          "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", "#1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "===", 
                      "2"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"l", "=", RowBox[{"CreateField", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                "d", ",", "\"L\""}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"r", "=", RowBox[{"CreateField", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                "d", ",", "\"R\""}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"m", "=", RowBox[{"CreateModel", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"l", ",", "r"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"m", "=", RowBox[{"AddModelTerm", "[", RowBox[{"m", ",", 
                RowBox[{"CoupleContractions", "[", RowBox[{"Contractions", 
                    "[", RowBox[{"m", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"l", ",", 
                          "r"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"mass", "=", RowBox[{"ExtractBilinearMatrix", "[", 
              RowBox[{RowBox[{"ModelExpression", "[", "m", "]"}], ",", "l", 
                ",", "r"}], "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"StringContainsQ", "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"PythonSource", "[", RowBox[{"ToPython", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"PrepareModelOutput", "[", RowBox[{"m", ",", 
                      RowBox[{"Association", "[", RowBox[{"\"M\"", "\[Rule]", 
                          "mass"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
              "\"def M(params, fields=None):\""}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], 
   "Input", CellTags -> "VerifiedExample"], Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], 
  Cell["Possible Issues", "ExampleSection"], Cell["Invalid input returns a \
structured Failure. Check FailureQ before using the result.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"FailureQ", "[", RowBox[{"ToPython", "[", 
        RowBox[{"PrepareModelOutput", "[", "\"x\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], 
   "Input", CellTags -> "VerifiedErrorExample"], 
  Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], Cell["Related Guides", 
   "MoreAboutSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Constructing finite groups", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
       {"../../Tutorials/ConstructingFiniteGroups.nb", None}]}], 
   "MoreAbout"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Metadata", "MetadataSection"], 
     Cell["Symbol", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Entity Type"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Paclet Name"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool`", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Context"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool/ref/ToPython", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "URI"]}, 
    Closed]]}, WindowTitle -> "ToPython \[LongDash] VVMFTool", 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 850}, TaggingRules -> <|"Paclet" -> "VVMFTool", 
